                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not convinced that 600 lines of shell is more maintainable than a few one-shot service files.  Can we make this simpler?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eldin Lee",
                        "email": "eldin.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "eldin-lee"
                    },
                    "message": "The goal of this PR was to use the new structured event defined in phosphor-dbus-interfaces. I attempted to unify the GPIO event handlers, but it ended up being too complex. I\u2019ll create a new PR with a simpler implementation based on the previous method."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/event-combo-failure-assert-success-deassert@.service",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "?  Why wouldn't this just be a dependency."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/event-combo-failure-assert-success-deassert@.service",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eldin Lee",
                        "email": "eldin.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "eldin-lee"
                    },
                    "message": "Ok, it probably makes more sense as a dependency. I\u2019ll switch to the traditional approach to implement it. Thanks for catching that."
                }
